r $x$ and the system of linear equations below, find the projection of $x$ onto the solution space of the system.\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}],\\,{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+9{x}_{2}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535940 true] [17592186375440 1113 #uuid "61cc989f-9d11-52b3-b431-d0b4753db895" 13194139535940 true] [17592186375440 1145 "First, we need to find a basis for the solution space of the system. \n\nConsider the augmented matrix $M$ of the system, which we reduce to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 9 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, there is $1$ pivot column (the $1$st one). Thus, ${x}_{2}$ is a free variable. From the first equation, we get ${x}_{1}=-3{x}_{2}.$ So, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-3{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]={x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nConsequently, $B={[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}$ is a basis of the solution space of the system. \n\nFinally, we find the projection of $x$ onto the solution space of the system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,x & =\\frac{x\\cdot b}{b\\cdot b}b \\\\  & =\\frac{(-4)\\cdot (-3)+8\\cdot 1}{{(-3)}^{2}+{1}^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{20}{10}b \\\\  & =2b \\\\  & =2[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535940 true] [17592186375441 1000 #edb/ref 17592186375442 13194139535940 true] [17592186375441 1000 #edb/ref 17592186375443 13194139535940 true] [17592186375441 1000 #edb/ref 17592186375444 13194139535940 true] [17592186375441 1000 #edb/ref 17592186375445 13194139535940 true] [17592186375441 1000 #edb/ref 17592186375446 13194139535940 true] [17592186375441 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535940 true] [1759218